-- title:
--   (51) — descent of $\Lambda^k$ (corrected: at a point of $\mathbb S_{MVIS}$, not $\mathbb S_{VIS}$; $u^{k-1}\in U$)
-- statement:
--   Let $E,F$ be finite-dimensional real inner product spaces, $U\subseteq E$ a closed convex set, $C\subseteq F$ a closed convex cone with dual cone $C^*=\{p:\langle x,p\rangle\ge0\ \forall x\in C\}$, and let $G:E\to E$, $J:E\to(-\infty,+\infty]$, $\Theta:E\to F$ satisfy the standing assumptions: $G$ is $L$-Lipschitz on $U$, $J$ is proper convex l.s.c., $\Theta$ is $C$-convex and $\tau$-Lipschitz on $U$ ($\tau>0$). Let the parameters satisfy $\frac{\sqrt5-1}{2}\le\eta<1$, $0<\gamma<1/\tau$, $0<\alpha\le\frac{1}{2(\gamma\tau^2+L+\tau)\eta}$, and let $\{(v^k,u^k,p^k,q^k)\}$ be generated by ALAVI (25)–(28) from arbitrary $u^1,v^0,p^1$.
--
--   Let $(u^\natural,p^\natural)$ be a solution of (MVIS). For every $k\ge2$ with $u^{k-1}\in U$,
--
--   $$
--   \Lambda^k(u^\natural,p^\natural)-\Lambda^{k+1}(u^\natural,p^\natural)\ge\rho\big[\|w^{k-1}-w^k\|^2+\|p^k-q^k\|^2\big],
--   $$
--
--   with $\Lambda^k$, $\rho$ and $\|w^{k-1}-w^k\|^2$ as in Lemma 4.1. Along a run, $\Lambda^k$ evaluated at a Minty point is nonincreasing from $k=3$ on.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: ℝⁿ and ℝᵐ with the Euclidean inner product → finite-dimensional real inner product spaces E, F; reason: ℝⁿ, ℝᵐ are instances and no coordinate is used, so the statement specializes to the page's
--   - generalization: G continuous on ℝⁿ and L-Lipschitz on U (H2); Θ continuous on ℝⁿ and τ-Lipschitz on an open O ⊇ U (H5) → G L-Lipschitz on U and Θ τ-Lipschitz on U, nothing assumed off U; reason: the proofs evaluate G and Θ only at points of U; the page's hypotheses imply these
--   - reading: J "a continuous function on U" (p.2) and "proper convex l.s.c." (H3, p.4) → J : E → (−∞, +∞] proper, convex, lower semicontinuous (IsProperConvexLSC); reason: the two printed descriptions differ; (H3) is the one the proofs use, and a convex J continuous on the closed set U, extended by +∞, satisfies it
--   - encoding: real values J(u) → (J u).toReal at points of dom J (effDom J); reason: J is finite wherever the statement evaluates it; at points outside dom J the printed inequalities read +∞ ≥ 0
--   - encoding: C a nonempty closed convex cone; C∗ (never defined on the page); Π the projection onto C∗ → C : ProperCone ℝ F; C∗ = ProperCone.innerDual C; Π = CalamaiMore.Convergence.proj onto C∗; reason: every nonempty closed convex cone is a ProperCone; C∗ is used as the dual cone {p | ⟨x, p⟩ ≥ 0 ∀ x ∈ C} (p.7, Example A.4); the projection onto the nonempty closed convex C∗ exists
--   - generalization: ALAVI input u¹, v⁰ ∈ ℝⁿ, p⁰ ∈ ℝᵐ, with p¹ read in (26) at k = 1 but never defined → u¹, v⁰ and p¹ arbitrary; reason: covers both readings p¹ = Π(p⁰ + γΘ(u¹)) and p¹ = p⁰
--   - correction: (u∗, p∗) ∈ S_VIS → (u♮, p♮) ∈ S_MVIS; reason: the step "Asm. B & Prop. 4" is the Minty inequality (20) at the point; at a point of S_VIS \ S_MVIS (51) fails: in the example of the mission description (ℝ² ≅ ℂ, C = ℝ₊, U = ℝ², J = 0, Θ(u) = |u| − 3, G(u) = g(|u|)·iu with g(r) = min(max(r − 1, −1), 1), η = 0.7, γ = 1/2, α = 0.1), Λᵏ(z, 0) with |z| = 1, a point of S_VIS, increases on 46% of the steps
--   - correction: k = 1, 2, … with u¹ ∈ ℝⁿ arbitrary → 2 ≤ k and uᵏ⁻¹ ∈ U; reason: at k = 1 the statement is undefined; at k = 2 the Lipschitz steps (42)–(43) need u¹ ∈ U, which the input does not give, and (51) is false without it: U = [0,1] ⊂ ℝ, C = ℝ₊, J = 0, Θ(u) = u, G(u) = −100·max(0, −1/2 − u) (zero on U, so L = 0), η = 0.7, γ = 1/2, α = 0.1, u¹ = −2, v⁰ = 0, p¹ = 2, (u, p) = (0, 0) ∈ S_MVIS give Λ²(0,0) − Λ³(0,0) = 3.87 < 4.87 = right-hand side; for k ≥ 3, uᵏ⁻¹ ∈ U holds automatically
--   - encoding: ‖wᵏ⁻¹ − wᵏ‖² for the stacked vector w = (v, u, p) → ‖vᵏ⁻¹ − vᵏ‖² + ‖uᵏ⁻¹ − uᵏ‖² + ‖pᵏ⁻¹ − pᵏ‖²; reason: the Euclidean norm of the stacked vector, written out
-- source:
--   Zhao, Zhu & Zhang, An Augmented Lagrangian Approach to Conically Constrained Non-monotone Variational Inequality Problems, arXiv:2306.01214v1, proof of Theorem 1 (i), display (51), p.18

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_Fixed_solutionSet
import Definitions.Def_CalamaiMore_Convergence_proj
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_Standing
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_Params
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_IsALAVIRun
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_IsMVIS
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_lam
import Definitions.Def_ALAVI_rho

namespace ALAVI

/-- **Display (51)** (corrected: at a point of `S_MVIS`, not `S_VIS`): descent of the Lyapunov
function. For `k ≥ 2` with `uᵏ⁻¹ ∈ U` and `(u♮, p♮)` a solution of (MVIS),
`Λᵏ(u♮, p♮) - Λᵏ⁺¹(u♮, p♮) ≥ ρ[‖wᵏ⁻¹ - wᵏ‖² + ‖pᵏ - qᵏ‖²]`.

Zhao, Zhu & Zhang, arXiv:2306.01214v1, proof of Theorem 1(i), (51), p.18.

Formalization Notes: the page takes `(u*, p*) ∈ S_VIS`, but its step "Asm. B & Prop. 4" is the
Minty inequality (20) at that point, which holds on `S_MVIS`, not on `S_VIS`; at a point of
`S_VIS \ S_MVIS` the inequality can fail (counterexample in the mission description). `k ≥ 2`
and `uᵏ⁻¹ ∈ U` as in Lemma 4.1. `‖wᵏ⁻¹ - wᵏ‖²` is the sum of three squares. -/
theorem eq_51 {E F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
    [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℝ F] [FiniteDimensional ℝ F]
    (U : Set E) (C : ProperCone ℝ F) (G : E → E) (J : E → EReal) (Θ : E → F) (L τ η α γ : ℝ) (v u : ℕ → E) (p q : ℕ → F)
    (hA : Standing U C G J Θ L τ) (hP : Params η α γ L τ)
    (hrun : IsALAVIRun U C G J Θ η α γ v u p q)
    (k : ℕ) (hk : 2 ≤ k) (hk1 : u (k - 1) ∈ U) (a : E) (b : F) (hab : IsMVIS U C G J Θ a b) :
    rho η α γ τ * (‖v (k - 1) - v k‖ ^ 2 + ‖u (k - 1) - u k‖ ^ 2 + ‖p (k - 1) - p k‖ ^ 2 +
          ‖p k - q k‖ ^ 2) ≤
      lam η α γ L τ v u p k a b - lam η α γ L τ v u p (k + 1) a b := by sorry

end ALAVI
